Infinispan OpenPGP Signing Key Statement
========================================

This file is the official, first-party statement of the OpenPGP keys used by this project to sign its release artifacts. It lives in the root of the infinispan/infinispan source repository so that it can be cited as a permanent reference (https://github.com/infinispan/infinispan/blob/main/KEYS). When signing keys are rotated, an updated version of this file will document both fingerprints and the transition between them. Until such a statement exists, signatures made with any other key should not be trusted for Infinispan artifacts.

Signing Key
-----------

Full fingerprint : F5FEBA84EB26C56457B2CF819E31AB27445478DB
Algorithm        : RSA 3072-bit (sign and certify)
User ID          : Infinispan <infinispan-maven@infinispan.org>
Valid from       : 2022-07-06
Expires on       : 2032-07-03

Scope of the Key
----------------

The key above signs:

* All artifacts published under groupId org.infinispan on Maven Central (https://central.sonatype.com/namespace/org.infinispan), including POM and JAR files. Each signature is published alongside its artifact as a file with an .asc extension; for example, infinispan-bom-16.1.4.pom.asc signs infinispan-bom-16.1.4.pom.
* Repository metadata of the Infinispan package repositories at https://download.jboss.org/infinispan/packages/ : repodata/repomd.xml for each YUM repository and Release.gpg / InRelease for the APT repository, so that clients can verify the integrity of those repositories (repo_gpgcheck=1 in yum/dnf; built-in verification by apt). Individual RPM and DEB packages are not GPG-signed.

Key Rotation
------------

No key rotation has occurred to date: this single key is the only OpenPGP key used for these coordinates, including org.infinispan:infinispan-bom releases 14.x through current 16.x. Releases published to Maven Central before July 2022 may carry no OpenPGP signature at all; they cannot be verified with any key and are not covered by this statement.

Verifying a Signature
---------------------

Import the public part of the signing key (included below, also available from https://download.jboss.org/infinispan/packages/signing.key) and verify an artifact:

  gpg --import KEYS
  gpg --verify infinispan-bom-16.1.4.pom.asc infinispan-bom-16.1.4.pom

A successful verification reports "Good signature from Infinispan <infinispan-maven@infinispan.org>" and lists the primary key fingerprint F5FE BA84 EB26 C564 57B2 CF81 9E31 AB27 4454 78DB.

